data.content:
Here are the recommended MSTest replacements:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetActiveUsers_ReturnsOnlyActiveUsers()
{
    var service = new UserService();
    var users = service.GetActiveUsers();

    // Assert.IsTrue(users.Count > 0)
    Assert.IsTrue(users.Count > 0); // or CollectionAssert.That.IsNotEmpty() in newer versions

    // Assert.IsTrue(users.All(u => u.IsActive))
    CollectionAssert.AllItemsAreNotNull(users);
    // For predicate checks, use:
    Assert.IsTrue(users.All(u => u.IsActive)); // no built-in equivalent

    // Assert.IsTrue(users.Count() == 3)
    Assert.AreEqual(3, users.Count);

    // Assert.IsTrue(admin != null)
    Assert.IsNotNull(users.Single(u => u.Role == "Admin"));
}
```

**Key MSTest collection assertions:**

| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| `Assert.IsTrue(x.Count > 0)` | `CollectionAssert.AreNotEqual(0, x.Count)` or keep `Assert.IsTrue` |
| `Assert.IsTrue(x.Count == n)` | `Assert.AreEqual(n, x.Count)` |
| `Assert.IsTrue(obj != null)` | `Assert.IsNotNull(obj)` |
| Checking two lists match | `CollectionAssert.AreEqual(expected, actual)` |
| Checking same items (any order) | `CollectionAssert.AreEquivalent(expected, actual)` |
| Checking item exists | `CollectionAssert.Contains(collection, item)` |
| All items match a type | `CollectionAssert.AllItemsAreInstancesOfType(col, typeof(T))` |

**Note:** MSTest's `CollectionAssert` doesn't have a built-in predicate-based "all items satisfy condition" assertion. For that, `Assert.IsTrue(collection.All(...))` is acceptable, or consider a library like **FluentAssertions** which gives you `users.Should().OnlyContain(u => u.IsActive)`.
